**Memo**

**To:** Executive Leadership Team  
**From:** Sarah Thompson, Director of Operations  
**Date:** March 15, 2024  
**Subject:** Strategic Overview of Drilling, Refining, and Pipeline Operations

---

As we progress through the fiscal year 2024, I would like to provide a comprehensive overview of our current operations in drilling, refining, pipeline management, exploration activities, and reserves assessment. This memo aims to consolidate our strategic initiatives and highlight key partnerships, challenges, and operational efficiencies that are pivotal for our sustained growth at Titan Oil & Gas.

### 1. Overview of Current Operations

Titan Oil & Gas, headquartered in Houston, Texas, has seen a robust increase in production levels over the past year, primarily driven by our operations in the Permian Basin, where we have identified several promising sites through our advanced seismic imaging technology provided by GeoTech Solutions. Currently, our production stands at approximately 250,000 barrels of oil equivalent per day (BOE/D), up from 220,000 BOE/D in 2023.

#### Drilling Operations

Our drilling operations are spearheaded by the Drilling Manager, Mark Johnson, and his team, which includes field engineers and geoscientists. As of March 2024, we have 15 active drilling rigs, primarily operated by Halliburton and Schlumberger, with a focus on horizontal drilling techniques that have proven effective in maximizing yield from our high-value shale formations.

In January 2024, we successfully completed the drilling of the Titan-34 well, which achieved an initial production rate of 1,200 BOE/D, surpassing our expectations. This accomplishment can be attributed to our recent investment in the latest rotary steerable systems (RSS) that enhance our drilling accuracy and reduce non-productive time.

### 2. Refining Capacity and Enhancements

Our refining capacity remains a cornerstone of our operations, with our flagship facility located in Port Arthur, Texas, managed by Refinery Manager Linda Gomez. The facility has a processing capacity of 350,000 barrels per day and specializes in producing ultra-low-sulfur diesel and high-octane gasoline.

In February 2024, we completed a $150 million upgrade to our hydrocracking unit, which was executed in collaboration with Jacobs Engineering. This upgrade is projected to increase our yield of high-value products by 10% and reduce emissions by 15% in compliance with the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) regulations.

### 3. Pipeline Infrastructure

The efficient transport of crude oil and refined products is critical to our operational success. Titan Oil & Gas operates an extensive pipeline network totaling over 1,200 miles, with major routes connecting our production sites in Texas to the Gulf Coast refineries.

Our pipeline operations are overseen by Pipeline Operations Director, Eric Chen, who has worked closely with the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) to ensure compliance with safety and environmental standards. In January 2024, we initiated the construction of the East Texas Pipeline Project, a $200 million investment that will enhance our transport capacity by 20% and facilitate the movement of crude oil from our new drilling sites in the East Texas Basin.

### 4. Exploration Initiatives

Our exploration efforts have been significantly bolstered by our partnership with the University of Texas at Austin, where Dr. Emily Carter leads a research team focusing on innovative exploratory techniques. In early 2024, we allocated $50 million towards advanced geological surveys and the acquisition of exploratory drilling rights in the Eagle Ford Shale region.

This exploratory initiative aligns with our goal to increase our proven reserves, which currently stand at approximately 1.5 billion barrels of oil equivalent, as reported in our Q4 2023 reserves audit by DeGolyer and MacNaughton.

### 5. Reserves Management

Effective reserves management is crucial for ensuring the longevity of our operations. Our reserves are regularly assessed and monitored through a combination of advanced data analytics and field testing. Senior Geologist, Tom Richards, has implemented a new reserves tracking system that integrates data from our drilling operations and production metrics.

As part of our commitment to sustainability, we are also exploring enhanced oil recovery (EOR) methods, specifically carbon dioxide injection techniques, in partnership with Occidental Petroleum. This collaborative effort aims to increase recovery rates from our existing fields, potentially adding an estimated 200 million barrels to our recoverable reserves.

### 6. Key Partnerships and Collaborations

Our success hinges on the strategic alliances we have established with various stakeholders in the industry. Notably, our relationship with Baker Hughes has been instrumental in optimizing our drilling operations through the provision of innovative technologies and services. Furthermore, our collaboration with the American Petroleum Institute (API) allows us to stay abreast of industry standards and regulatory changes.

We are also engaged with local communities and environmental groups to ensure our operations are conducted responsibly. Our Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) initiatives, which include investments in local education and environmental conservation projects, have fostered goodwill and strengthened our community relations.

### 7. Challenges and Risk Management

Despite our successes, we face several challenges that require ongoing attention. Volatility in oil prices, driven by geopolitical tensions and shifts in global demand, remains a significant risk. As of March 2024, Brent crude is trading at approximately $85 per barrel, influenced by supply chain disruptions in Eastern Europe.

Additionally, regulatory changes and environmental concerns necessitate a proactive approach to risk management. Our Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) team, led by Sarah Miller, is continuously assessing our operations to ensure compliance with state and federal regulations while minimizing our environmental footprint.

### 8. Future Outlook

Looking ahead, our strategic focus will remain on enhancing operational efficiencies, expanding our drilling footprint, and increasing our refining capabilities. We anticipate that our investment in digital technologies will further streamline operations and improve decision-making processes.

Our projected increase in production to 300,000 BOE/D by Q4 2024 is contingent on the successful execution of our drilling program and the timely completion of pipeline projects. We will continue to evaluate emerging markets and potential acquisitions that can bolster our portfolio and position us for future growth.

### Conclusion

In conclusion, Titan Oil & Gas is well-positioned for continued success in the competitive landscape of the oil and gas industry. Our commitment to operational excellence, sustainable practices, and strategic partnerships will enable us to navigate challenges and seize opportunities as they arise. I look forward to discussing these initiatives further in our upcoming board meeting on April 5, 2024.

Thank you for your attention and support.

